  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Detection reports (226 across 186 functions) and developer confirmations (60 on the NVIDIA forum, 26.5%) are distinct denominators; the paper omits per-library and per-category confirmation counts and does not report GPU-NBDetect's own false-positive count.",
    "NVIDIA developers noted that rounding discrepancies flagged against CPU C math.h can still lie within CUDA's documented ULP tolerance bounds rather than constituting formal CUDA spec violations.",
    "GPU-NBDetect supports only float (FP32) and double (FP64) scalar math APIs across 4 libraries on a single GPU generation (GTX 1080 Ti, CUDA 11.1); FP16, BF16, Decimal64/128, Operator bugs, and Device-specific latency inversions (Strategies 7-9) are excluded from Tables 5-6.",
    "Assertion thresholds (1e-7, 0.9, 0.01, 2.5x/3x) are fixed heuristics not scaled by ULP; the authors acknowledge timing strategies (S7-S9) can produce false positives and mutation operators introduce run-to-run randomness.",
    "Internal PDF printing discrepancies documented transparently: Table 2 Data Type + Operator sums to 237 (143+94, matching total 397) while Table 1 F-4 and Section 4.2 state 239 (59.6%); Table 6 CuPy RS counts sum to 18 while Total prints 16; Table 4 Row 2 prints 'or' instead of 'and' for subnormal underflow; Section 5.3 calls the mutators 'seven mutation operators' while listing eight bullets."
  ],
